# profiles.http — try every /api/profiles route. Run in order.
# BEFORE YOU START:
#   1. npm run seed:profiles   → copy the 4 printed ids into the variables below
#   2. Make sure mira.demo@example.com exists (request 3 creates it if not)

@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000/api
@junId = PASTE_JUN_ID_HERE
@samId = PASTE_SAM_ID_HERE
@ashId = PASTE_ASH_ID_HERE
@newId = PASTE_NEW_ID_HERE

### 1. Options → 200 (works without logging in)
GET {{baseUrl}}/profiles/options

### 2. Log out first, then: my profile → 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/profiles/me

### 3. Create Mira (a 409 here just means she already exists, which is fine)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "mira.demo@example.com",
  "username": "mira_demo",
  "password": "tea under the willow",
  "birthDate": "1998-04-12",
  "agreeToGuidelines": true
}

### 4. Log in as Mira
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "mira.demo@example.com", "password": "tea under the willow" }

### 5. My profile → 200 (created automatically, mostly empty, with privacy defaults)
GET {{baseUrl}}/profiles/me

### 6. Update several things → 200
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/profiles/me
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "displayName": "Mira (demo)",
  "pronouns": "she/her",
  "avatar": "moon",
  "bio": "New to the city. I like quiet cafés, long walks and swapping book recommendations.",
  "interests": ["reading", "tea", "journaling"],
  "languages": ["en", "fr"],
  "conversationStyle": "slow-thoughtful",
  "friendshipGoals": ["chat-buddy", "hobby-buddy"]
}

### 7. Update ONE thing → 200 (everything else stays the same)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/profiles/me
Content-Type: application/json

{ "bio": "Quiet cafés and book swaps, please ☕📚" }

### 8. Made-up interest → 400, details.interests
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/profiles/me
Content-Type: application/json

{ "interests": ["reading", "skydiving-at-midnight"] }

### 9. Too many interests → 400
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/profiles/me
Content-Type: application/json

{ "interests": ["reading","tea","coffee","baking","cooking","houseplants","puzzles","board-games","drawing","painting","writing"] }

### 10. Sneaky fields → 200, but isComplete stays false and "user" is unchanged 🔒
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/profiles/me
Content-Type: application/json

{ "bio": "Still me.", "isComplete": true, "user": "000000000000000000000000" }

### 11. Empty update → 400 "There's nothing to update yet."
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/profiles/me
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 12. Change ONE privacy setting → 200 (the other five stay the same)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/profiles/me
Content-Type: application/json

{ "privacy": { "showPronouns": false } }

### 13. Preview my public profile → pronouns now null, no privacy settings, no dates
GET {{baseUrl}}/profiles/me/public

### 14. Clear my conversation style with null → 200
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/profiles/me
Content-Type: application/json

{ "conversationStyle": null, "privacy": { "showPronouns": true } }

### 15. Jun's profile → 200: communities = [] (hidden by Jun's privacy), no user id, no dates
GET {{baseUrl}}/profiles/{{junId}}

### 16. Sam's profile → 200: pronouns = null, communities shown
GET {{baseUrl}}/profiles/{{samId}}

### 17. Ash (hidden from Discover) → 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/profiles/{{ashId}}

### 18. New (onboarding not finished) → 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/profiles/{{newId}}

### 19. Badly formed id → 400 "That profile link doesn't look right."
GET {{baseUrl}}/profiles/hello-there

### 20. Well-formed id that doesn't exist → 404 (the same message as 17 and 18)
GET {{baseUrl}}/profiles/000000000000000000000000

### 21. Log out, then Jun's profile → 401 (profiles are for members only)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/profiles/{{junId}}